  "title": "Infinite carousel, desktop: every trip glides forward to the right slide and never back, across the seam both ways, with arrows, keys, dots and three clicks in a row; a query, a two-row grid and a single slide",
  "description": "Infinite estrategia-web/carousel (0.5.0 loop, true by default; 0.6.0 infinite; 0.7.2 glide) on /prueba-carrusel-bucle/ at 1200: (1) «Carrusel con una de más», 3 slides with 2.4 in view like Lavandería's home page (SEEN FAILING on 06-10-2026 with 0.7.1: the order changed and scrollLeft jumped to 0) — a full lap forward plus one, back across the seam, three «next» in a row; (2) «Carrusel en bucle», 5 with 2 in view and the loop by default — both arrows enabled on load, no repeated ids, a lap forward plus one (the active dot follows; on the last one the first peeks in right after it), back across the seam, dot 1 from the last, ← on the first and →, a dot leads to its slide, three in a row; (3) a Query: six dots, wrapping both ways with arrows and keys; (4) the two-row grid wraps by columns and no card changes row; (5) a single slide: static, nothing reordered. Each trip is recorded frame by frame by probes.js and checked: right slide, never back, glides (≥ 3 frames per slide, no jump over half a slide), nothing left behind, same number of slides. Every wait is a FACT. Read by browser-carousel-infinite. It was carousel-infinite.test.mjs (sections 1-5, level 3) until 29-10-2026.",
